.TH DAYLIGHT 1 "2026-11-08" "Daylight 5.0.0-rc.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
daylight \- local management and utilities for Daylight GNU/Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B daylight
COMMAND [OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Daylight adds an isolated desktop session and local utilities to Debian or Raspberry Pi OS.
It does not replace the base OS identity, edit existing shell configuration, or enable telemetry by default.
.SH COMMANDS
Run daylight --help for the complete command list.
Status, info, doctor and monitor are read-only. Passwords are generated using the Linux kernel CSPRNG.
Package update and remove use APT for Daylight packages only; they never run autoremove.
Desktop settings live under XDG_CONFIG_HOME/daylight, falling back to ~/.config/daylight.
.SH PRIVACY
Opening a terminal sends no network request. Optional boot events require explicit activation and a configured HTTPS collector.
Events count boots, not unique users. Transport providers necessarily see a source IP.
